1
00:00:01,569 --> 00:00:02,801
    - PREVIOUSLY ON<i> HAVEN...</i>    

2
00:00:02,870 --> 00:00:04,236
    - YOU'VE BEEN FALSIFYING    
         POLICE REPORTS.        

3
00:00:04,305 --> 00:00:07,139
     - I'VE BEEN DOING WHAT     
   WE'VE ALWAYS DONE IN HAVEN.  

4
00:00:07,208 --> 00:00:08,941
    - WE'RE GONNA BE LOOKING    
  FOR A NEW CHIEF IMMEDIATELY.  

5
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:11,810
     - SOMEONE WANTS ME OUT?    
     IT'S THE REV, ISN'T IT?    

6
00:00:11,879 --> 00:00:13,479
     - HE WANTS TO BE CHIEF?    

7
00:00:13,547 --> 00:00:15,481
      - HE WANTS TO CONTROL     
           WHOEVER IS.          

8
00:00:15,549 --> 00:00:17,316
       - YOU ARE AMAZING.       

9
00:00:17,385 --> 00:00:19,785
       I WANT YOU, AUDREY,      
       BECAUSE YOU'RE YOU.      

10
00:00:19,854 --> 00:00:21,987
         - THIS IS EVI.         
       - I'M DUKE'S WIFE.       

11
00:00:22,056 --> 00:00:23,889
     WHY ARE YOU EVEN HERE?     
         - IT'S MY DAD.         

12
00:00:23,958 --> 00:00:26,125
         THE OLD BASTARD        
          MADE ME SWEAR         

13
00:00:26,193 --> 00:00:27,993
   THAT I WOULD COME BACK HERE  
 IF THE TROUBLES EVER RETURNED. 

14
00:00:28,062 --> 00:00:30,129
        AND THEN HE DIED.       

15
00:00:30,197 --> 00:00:32,531
- DUKE DOESN'T SUSPECT ANYTHING?
              - NO.             

16
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:35,167
      AND NOW THAT HE KNOWS     
    HIS FATHER WAS MURDERED,    

17
00:00:35,236 --> 00:00:36,535
         YOU'VE GOT HIM.        

18
00:00:36,604 --> 00:00:38,537
          - [chuckles]          

19
00:00:46,781 --> 00:00:49,581
          - HI, CATHY.          
  HOW'S YOUR LITTLE MAN TODAY?  

20
00:00:53,287 --> 00:00:55,454
     GOOD TO SEE YA, MARTHA.    

21
00:01:03,564 --> 00:01:04,897
      - NOT THE FIRST TIME      

22
00:01:04,965 --> 00:01:08,534
        WE'VE CAUGHT YOU        
 BREAKING AND ENTERING, DWIGHT. 

23
00:01:08,602 --> 00:01:10,836
          - CAUGHT ME?          

24
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:12,871
          CHIEF WUORNOS         
       CAN CLEAR THIS UP.       

25
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:15,541
      - YOU HAVEN'T HEARD.      

26
00:01:15,609 --> 00:01:18,544
  WUORNOS ISN'T CHIEF ANYMORE.  
        WE GOT A NEW GUY.       

27
00:01:18,612 --> 00:01:21,213
           SO NO MORE           
    SPECIAL TREATMENT FOR...    

28
00:01:21,282 --> 00:01:23,816
         SPECIAL PEOPLE,        
            YOU KNOW?           

29
00:01:24,819 --> 00:01:26,151
       - ARE YOU SWEATIN'?      

30
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:29,221
      - IT'S WARM OUT HERE.     
     - I WOULDN'T SAY THAT.     

31
00:01:30,257 --> 00:01:33,358
            - DWIGHT.           

32
00:01:33,427 --> 00:01:35,394
          WHAT'S THIS?          

33
00:01:35,463 --> 00:01:38,230
    - DID A LITTLE CLEANUP AT   
 THE CENTRAL COAST MEAT PACKING.

34
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,833
       - WITH A CROSSBOW?       

35
00:01:42,436 --> 00:01:44,603
           I GOT THIS           
         FROM NOW, PAUL.        

36
00:01:46,774 --> 00:01:48,207
             - FINE.            

37
00:01:48,275 --> 00:01:50,075
             - PAUL.            

38
00:01:51,445 --> 00:01:53,412
             CUFFS.             

39
00:02:04,291 --> 00:02:06,058
    - SO THERE'S A NEW CHIEF?   

40
00:02:06,127 --> 00:02:08,694
      - YEAH. THE SELECTMAN     
    SENT IN THIS GUY MERRILL.   

41
00:02:08,762 --> 00:02:10,362
         HE'S A REFORMER        
         FROM BRUNSWICK,        

42
00:02:10,431 --> 00:02:12,498
    AND I THINK HE'S CLUELESS   
       ABOUT THE TROUBLES.      

43
00:02:12,566 --> 00:02:13,665
      - WON'T BE FOR LONG.      

44
00:02:13,734 --> 00:02:15,567
          - SPRINKLES?          

45
00:02:15,636 --> 00:02:17,903
           - OH, YEAH.          

46
00:02:17,972 --> 00:02:20,339
          - JUST WATCH          
   WHERE YOU POINT THIS THING.  

47
00:02:41,228 --> 00:02:43,896
       - WHAT DID I CATCH       
         IN THAT PLACE?         

48
00:02:49,603 --> 00:02:51,937
         WHAT THE HELL?         

49
00:02:53,274 --> 00:02:54,706
             [thud]             

50
00:03:16,797 --> 00:03:18,130
          - ALL RIGHT,          
         SO YOU'RE OKAY         

51
00:03:18,199 --> 00:03:20,365
           WITH TAKING          
  THE GRAVEYARD SHIFT TONIGHT?  

52
00:03:20,434 --> 00:03:24,403
  - MM-HMM. IT'S GONNA BE GOOD. 
       I'M NOT IN CHARGE.       

53
00:03:24,471 --> 00:03:27,906
     AND MOST OF HAVEN'S UP     
   AT THE BOAT PARADE, SO GO.   

54
00:03:27,975 --> 00:03:29,942
          GO ON YOUR--          
           YOUR DATE.           

55
00:03:30,010 --> 00:03:31,643
       - IT'S NOT A DATE.       
           - OH, SURE.          

56
00:03:31,712 --> 00:03:33,579
      OF COURSE. THAT'S WHY     
 I'VE NEVER SEEN YOU SO NERVOUS.

57
00:03:33,647 --> 00:03:35,247
    BECAUSE OF YOUR NON-DATE.   

58
00:03:35,316 --> 00:03:36,915
    - IT'S JUST--IT'S BEEN--    

59
00:03:36,984 --> 00:03:39,751
    IT'S BEEN, WHAT, A MONTH    
  SINCE CHRIS LEFT FOR LONDON,  

60
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:43,388
   AND HIS TROUBLE WAS STILL,   
    YOU KNOW, RELATIVELY NEW.   

61
00:03:43,457 --> 00:03:44,723
            - RIGHT,            
      AND PEOPLE SEE CHRIS      

62
00:03:44,792 --> 00:03:47,559
        AND THEN THEY'RE        
       IMMEDIATELY VERY...      

63
00:03:47,628 --> 00:03:49,061
          FOND OF HIM.          

64
00:03:49,129 --> 00:03:51,630
          IT'S NOTHING          
         TO WORRY ABOUT.        

65
00:03:51,699 --> 00:03:54,066
              - NO?             
              - NO.             

66
00:03:54,134 --> 00:03:55,234
          - [chuckles]          
               NO.              

67
00:03:55,302 --> 00:03:56,902
         - GOT A VISITOR        
         UP FRONT, HON'.        

68
00:03:56,971 --> 00:04:00,239
            - THANKS.           
  - FOR NATHAN. CROCKER'S HERE. 

69
00:04:09,016 --> 00:04:11,083
     - YOU KNOW THAT I HATE     
    THAT YOU'RE A COP, RIGHT?   

70
00:04:11,151 --> 00:04:13,085
             - YEAH.            
             - YEAH.            

71
00:04:13,153 --> 00:04:14,953
        AND THAT I THINK        
         IT'S RIDICULOUS        

72
00:04:15,022 --> 00:04:16,755
        THAT THEY PUT YOU       
    IN CHARGE OF THIS PLACE.    

73
00:04:16,824 --> 00:04:18,457
            - UH-HUH.           

74
00:04:18,525 --> 00:04:21,460
  - BUT FOR CERTAIN REASONS...  

75
00:04:21,528 --> 00:04:22,861
         IT MAKES SENSE.        

76
00:04:22,930 --> 00:04:25,998
    - WELL, I'M NOT THE CHIEF   
     ANYMORE, YOU REMEMBER?     

77
00:04:26,066 --> 00:04:27,699
             - YEAH.            

78
00:04:31,238 --> 00:04:35,340
    BUT DO YOU WANNA KNOW WHY   
  YOU'RE NOT THE CHIEF ANYMORE? 

79
00:04:35,409 --> 00:04:37,476
              EVI.              

80
00:04:37,544 --> 00:04:39,344
     SHE TIPPED OFF THE REV     
         ABOUT YOUR FILE        

81
00:04:39,413 --> 00:04:41,513
     ON THE TROUBLED PEOPLE.    

82
00:04:41,582 --> 00:04:44,082
            I SAW IT            
          ON HER PHONE.         

83
00:04:45,386 --> 00:04:48,186
            - I KNEW            
         IT WAS THE REV.        

84
00:04:48,255 --> 00:04:50,689
        BUT HOW THE HELL        
        IS EVI INVOLVED?        

85
00:04:50,758 --> 00:04:53,525
          - YOU GOT ME.         
    I MEAN, THINK HOW I FEEL.   

86
00:04:53,594 --> 00:04:55,027
       I'M MARRIED TO HER.      

87
00:04:55,095 --> 00:04:57,596
    GOD ONLY KNOWS WHAT ELSE    
          SHE'S HIDING.         

88
00:05:00,067 --> 00:05:01,833
             LOOK...            

89
00:05:01,902 --> 00:05:06,038
    I FIGURE WE DO THIS HERE.   
      OTHERWISE SHE'D BOLT.     

90
00:05:06,106 --> 00:05:08,206
           I TOLD HER           
    THAT YOU WERE HELPING ME    

91
00:05:08,275 --> 00:05:10,542
    WITH MY PARKING TICKETS.    

92
00:05:10,611 --> 00:05:12,177
         IT WAS THE BEST        
      I COULD COME UP WITH.     

93
00:05:12,246 --> 00:05:14,379
          - HMM. OKAY.          

94
00:05:14,448 --> 00:05:16,782
          LET'S PUT HER         
       IN THE BREAK ROOM.       

95
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:20,952
             - UM...            

96
00:05:23,424 --> 00:05:25,590
     WHAT THE HELL IS THAT?     

97
00:05:28,996 --> 00:05:33,031
     - DID DUKE FINALLY PAY     
      HIS PARKING TICKETS?      

98
00:05:34,101 --> 00:05:35,600
            MM. OH...           

99
00:05:36,970 --> 00:05:38,670
             CHRIS.             

100
00:05:38,739 --> 00:05:41,506
          - OH, RIGHT.          
           WORKPLACE.           

101
00:05:41,575 --> 00:05:42,808
             - YEAH.            

102
00:05:46,313 --> 00:05:49,247
            - I GUESS           
       I JUST DON'T CARE.       

103
00:05:49,316 --> 00:05:51,450
     - OKAY, HEY, HEY, HEY.     
             - WHAT?            

104
00:05:51,518 --> 00:05:53,085
          - WHY DON'T I         
       JUST GRAB MY STUFF,      

105
00:05:53,153 --> 00:05:56,788
       AND THEN WE CAN GO       
         TO THE PARADE?         

106
00:05:56,857 --> 00:05:59,124
            - PARADE?           

107
00:05:59,193 --> 00:06:00,959
     WITH BOATS, AND LIGHTS,    

108
00:06:01,028 --> 00:06:02,694
    AND DRINKING, AND PEOPLE?   

109
00:06:02,763 --> 00:06:04,496
             - YEAH.            
              - NO.             

110
00:06:04,565 --> 00:06:07,432
        I DON'T WANNA SEE       
         ANYONE BUT YOU.        

111
00:06:07,501 --> 00:06:10,635
     - PARKER, YOU'D BETTER     
          GET OUT HERE.         

112
00:06:10,704 --> 00:06:11,970
          - I GOTTA...          

113
00:06:12,039 --> 00:06:13,638
            - NO, NO,           
          WE GOT PLANS.         

114
00:06:13,707 --> 00:06:15,340
         THIS BETTER NOT        
          BE IMPORTANT.         

115
00:06:15,409 --> 00:06:16,775
             [sighs]            

116
00:06:16,844 --> 00:06:19,678
         I LOVE THAT YOU        
       DON'T LISTEN TO ME!      

117
00:06:23,684 --> 00:06:25,550
     - IS THAT BLACK BLOOD?     

118
00:06:29,790 --> 00:06:31,523
      THAT'S OFFICER STARK.     

119
00:06:36,630 --> 00:06:38,897
          - HE'S DEAD.          

120
00:06:41,535 --> 00:06:44,002
          [folk music]          

121
00:06:44,071 --> 00:06:52,077
               � �              

122
00:07:16,670 --> 00:07:18,470
        - I JUST SAW HIM.       

123
00:07:18,539 --> 00:07:21,473
         HE LOOKED PALE         
      AND SWEATY, BUT NOT--     

124
00:07:21,542 --> 00:07:23,642
         - NOT AS DEAD?         

125
00:07:23,710 --> 00:07:26,778
            'CAUSE...           
        HE'S PRETTY DEAD.       

126
00:07:26,847 --> 00:07:28,246
     - LOOK, HIS VEINS ARE--    

127
00:07:28,315 --> 00:07:29,815
         THEY'RE BLACK.         

128
00:07:31,452 --> 00:07:34,085
         - WHAT THE HELL        
            IS THIS?            

129
00:07:34,154 --> 00:07:36,254
           IS THAT ONE          
         OF MY OFFICERS?        

130
00:07:37,491 --> 00:07:39,357
     - THAT'S CHIEF MERRILL.    

131
00:07:40,828 --> 00:07:44,830
       - AND WHO ARE YOU?       
            - I AM...           

132
00:07:45,866 --> 00:07:47,632
             NOBODY.            

133
00:07:49,203 --> 00:07:51,803
       - WHAT DO YOU THINK      
COULD CAUSE SOMETHING LIKE THIS?

134
00:07:51,872 --> 00:07:53,004
            - [sighs]           

135
00:07:53,073 --> 00:07:55,106
   - MAYBE A CHEMICAL WEAPON.   

136
00:07:55,175 --> 00:07:57,509
      - WE'RE NOT A TARGET      
     FOR ANYTHING LIKE THAT.    

137
00:07:57,578 --> 00:08:00,645
     - WE MAY WANNA CONSIDER    
      OTHER POSSIBILITIES.      

138
00:08:00,714 --> 00:08:03,748
   - ARE YOU SAYING THIS TOWN   
DOESN'T HAVE ANY LOCAL FANATICS?

139
00:08:03,817 --> 00:08:06,751
 GROUPS WITH A REASON TO TARGET 
  THE HAVEN POLICE DEPARTMENT?  

140
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,654
       I SUGGEST YOU LOOK       
      INTO THAT RIGHT NOW.      

141
00:08:11,225 --> 00:08:14,226
     [indistinct chattering]    

142
00:08:16,196 --> 00:08:17,629
   - THIS ISN'T THE PENTAGON.   

143
00:08:17,698 --> 00:08:20,298
        WHO'S GONNA STAGE       
   A CHEMICAL ATTACK IN HAVEN?  

144
00:08:20,367 --> 00:08:21,967
     - THE MORE PEOPLE KNOW     
       ABOUT THE TROUBLED,      

145
00:08:22,035 --> 00:08:24,102
ARE.                            

146
00:08:25,305 --> 00:08:27,272
     - DO YOU THINK THE REV     
      IS WHIPPING THEM UP?      

147
00:08:27,341 --> 00:08:29,641
       - DUKE JUST TOLD ME      
   THAT THE REV GOT ME FIRED.   

148
00:08:29,710 --> 00:08:31,309
      - ARE YOU KIDDING ME?     

149
00:08:31,378 --> 00:08:33,211
        - I KNEW HE'D TRY       
   AND GET ME OUT EVENTUALLY.   

150
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:35,313
     IT JUST HAPPENED SOONER    
        THAN I EXPECTED.        

151
00:08:35,382 --> 00:08:38,517
          - ALL RIGHT,          
   SO THE REV GETS HIS CHIEF.   

152
00:08:38,585 --> 00:08:40,285
           WHY ATTACK           
       THE DEPARTMENT NOW?      

153
00:08:40,354 --> 00:08:43,188
  - UNLESS THE PERP IS SOMEONE  
     UNHAPPY ABOUT MERRILL.     

154
00:08:43,257 --> 00:08:45,524
       - YOU GET REPLACED.      
     YOU DO HAVE YOUR FANS.     

155
00:08:45,592 --> 00:08:48,226
           - YOU THINK          
    IT'S SOMEONE PRO-TROUBLED   

156
00:08:48,295 --> 00:08:50,762
     WITH TECHNICAL KNOWHOW,    

157
00:08:50,831 --> 00:08:52,797
     ACCESS TO CHEMICALS...     

158
00:08:52,866 --> 00:08:54,633
         THE LAST PERSON        
    PAUL ARRESTED WAS DWIGHT.   

159
00:08:54,701 --> 00:08:56,034
             - YEAH,            
       YOUR DAD'S CLEANER.      

160
00:08:56,103 --> 00:08:58,236
      WE REALLY DON'T KNOW      
      THAT MUCH ABOUT HIM.      

161
00:08:58,305 --> 00:09:00,906
          - HE'S DEAD?          
    - MAYBE YOU HAD A GRUDGE.   

162
00:09:00,974 --> 00:09:04,109
   - NATHAN, LISTEN, I DIDN'T   
 DO ANYTHING TO THAT GUY, OKAY? 

163
00:09:04,177 --> 00:09:05,577
         YOU REALLY NEED        
      TO START TRUSTING ME.     

164
00:09:05,646 --> 00:09:06,945
       WITH THE NEW CHIEF       
            IN TOWN,            

165
00:09:07,014 --> 00:09:08,547
        YOU MIGHT NEED ME       
         MORE THAN EVER.        

166
00:09:10,851 --> 00:09:13,351
             [sighs]            

167
00:09:15,589 --> 00:09:17,289
   - WE'RE GONNA DO THIS NOW?   

168
00:09:17,357 --> 00:09:20,425
             - WAIT.            
              EVI.              

169
00:09:20,494 --> 00:09:22,694
            SHOW HIM            
       WHAT YOU SHOWED ME.      

170
00:09:36,076 --> 00:09:38,009
         - IT STARTS AT         
        THE EXTREMITIES.        

171
00:09:38,078 --> 00:09:40,045
       - WE GOTTA GET HER       
        TO THE HOSPITAL.        

172
00:09:40,113 --> 00:09:42,147
       - HOW LONG HAS SHE       
         BEEN LIKE THIS?        

173
00:09:42,215 --> 00:09:44,416
          - EXCUSE ME.          
   SHE'S STANDING RIGHT HERE.   

174
00:09:44,484 --> 00:09:46,117
             - DUKE,            
        WHAT'S HAPPENING?       

175
00:09:46,186 --> 00:09:48,587
   - WERE YOU AND PARKER ABLE   
 TO LOCATE THE CHEMICAL SOURCE? 

176
00:09:48,655 --> 00:09:49,955
       - NO, NOT YET, SIR.      

177
00:09:50,023 --> 00:09:52,257
         - DID YOU HAVE         
       ANY DIRECT CONTACT       

178
00:09:52,326 --> 00:09:53,625
       WITH OFFICER STARK?      

179
00:09:53,694 --> 00:09:55,360
         SHAKE HIS HAND,        
   SIT AT HIS DESK, ANYTHING?   

180
00:09:55,429 --> 00:09:57,128
              - NO.             

181
00:09:57,197 --> 00:09:58,463
        - BUT THIS THING        
        KEEPS SPREADING.        

182
00:09:58,532 --> 00:10:01,833
   SO IT'S GOTTA BE BIOLOGICAL  
          AND AIRBORNE.         

183
00:10:01,902 --> 00:10:03,602
             - SIR.             

184
00:10:03,670 --> 00:10:05,403
   - MA'AM, I'LL NEED YOU BACK  
  IN THE BREAK ROOM RIGHT NOW.  

185
00:10:05,472 --> 00:10:07,138
     - WAIT A MINUTE, CHIEF.    
             - NOW!             

186
00:10:10,644 --> 00:10:12,077
      LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,     

187
00:10:12,145 --> 00:10:14,713
 WE MAY HAVE A BIOLOGICAL AGENT 
        IN THE BUILDING,        

188
00:10:14,781 --> 00:10:17,582
           WHICH MEANS          
      WE FOLLOW PROCEDURE.      

189
00:10:17,651 --> 00:10:19,250
         WE CANNOT ALLOW        
        THE CONTAMINATION       

190
00:10:19,319 --> 00:10:20,685
       TO SPREAD FURTHER.       

191
00:10:20,754 --> 00:10:23,655
     SO UNTIL THIS SITUATION    
      IS RESOLVED, NOBODY--     

192
00:10:23,724 --> 00:10:25,490
       AND I MEAN<i> NOBODY--</i>      

193
00:10:25,559 --> 00:10:27,258
         GOES IN OR OUT         
        OF THIS BUILDING.       

194
00:10:27,327 --> 00:10:30,061
    THE HAVEN POLICE STATION    
    IS NOW UNDER QUARANTINE.    

195
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:32,263
       THIS IS A LOCKDOWN.      

196
00:10:32,332 --> 00:10:35,100
        [dramatic music]        

197
00:10:35,168 --> 00:10:40,205
               � �              

198
00:10:42,676 --> 00:10:44,809
   - THIS THING IS CONTAINED.   
           ABSOLUTELY.          

199
00:10:44,878 --> 00:10:47,045
  NO ONE'S LEAVING THE BUILDING 
        UNTIL IT'S CLEAR.       

200
00:10:48,949 --> 00:10:51,149
        I'LL DO WHATEVER        
         HAS TO BE DONE.        

201
00:10:53,387 --> 00:10:55,120
           COPY THAT.           

202
00:10:55,188 --> 00:10:57,889
           I'LL AWAIT           
      FURTHER INSTRUCTION.      

203
00:11:01,528 --> 00:11:04,229
   - WHAT DO THE STATE POLICE   
          HAVE TO SAY?          

204
00:11:06,233 --> 00:11:08,967
       - THAT WE'RE DOING       
        THE RIGHT THING.        

205
00:11:09,036 --> 00:11:12,037
   THE CONTAGION HASN'T SPREAD  
   BEYOND THE POLICE STATION.   

206
00:11:14,041 --> 00:11:15,607
          - ALL RIGHT.          

207
00:11:15,676 --> 00:11:18,343
   LIKE YOU ASKED, IT'S A LIST  
   OF EVERYONE IN THE STATION.  

208
00:11:18,412 --> 00:11:20,245
       IT'S A SMALL GROUP.      

209
00:11:21,682 --> 00:11:24,315
       - HUGH UNDERWOOD--       
         HE'S A DOCTOR?         

210
00:11:24,384 --> 00:11:26,484
- HE SAID HE'D LOOK AT THE BODY,
       CHECK ON THE SICK.       

211
00:11:26,553 --> 00:11:29,254
             - GOOD.            

212
00:11:29,322 --> 00:11:32,123
        HAVE THE OFFICERS       
    KEEP AN EYE ON EVERYBODY.   

213
00:11:32,192 --> 00:11:34,492
   - SIR, THE PEOPLE OUT THERE  
   ARE SCARED FOR THEIR LIVES.  

214
00:11:34,561 --> 00:11:35,827
         - WELL, THAT'S         
         TO BE EXPECTED.        

215
00:11:35,896 --> 00:11:37,662
       THAT'S WHY WE HAVE       
       TO MAINTAIN ORDER.       

216
00:11:37,731 --> 00:11:39,497
        I PUT LOCK CODES        
        ON ALL THE DOORS.       

217
00:11:39,566 --> 00:11:42,467
        ALL THE LANDLINES       
         ARE SHUT DOWN.         

218
00:11:42,536 --> 00:11:44,836
    I WANT YOU TO CONFISCATE    
     EVERYBODY'S CELL PHONE.    

219
00:11:44,905 --> 00:11:47,105
    - PEOPLE WILL WANNA STAY    
  IN TOUCH WITH THEIR FAMILIES. 

220
00:11:47,174 --> 00:11:48,573
       - AND I'LL NEED YOU      
 AND THE REST OF THE DEPARTMENT 

221
00:11:48,642 --> 00:11:49,908
   TO SURRENDER YOUR WEAPONS.   

222
00:11:49,976 --> 00:11:51,576
             - WHAT?            
 - THEY'LL BE PLACED IN A LOCKER

223
00:11:51,645 --> 00:11:53,378
          UNDER MY OWN          
      PERSONAL ACCESS CODE.     

224
00:11:53,447 --> 00:11:55,046
         WE CAN'T AFFORD        
       SOMEONE PANICKING,       

225
00:11:55,115 --> 00:11:56,848
      DOING SOMETHING RASH.     

226
00:11:58,285 --> 00:12:00,952
      THIS ISN'T OPTIONAL.      

227
00:12:16,136 --> 00:12:17,602
     - WE CAN LEAVE ANYTIME.    

228
00:12:17,671 --> 00:12:19,170
          I'LL JUST USE         
      MY IRRESISTIBLE CHARM     

229
00:12:19,239 --> 00:12:20,505
        ON YOUR NEW BOSS.       

230
00:12:20,574 --> 00:12:22,040
       - IT'S RESISTIBLE.       

231
00:12:25,378 --> 00:12:26,778
      - WHAT ARE YOU DOING?     

232
00:12:26,847 --> 00:12:28,446
    - JUST A LITTLE INSURANCE   
       IN CASE, YOU KNOW,       

233
00:12:28,515 --> 00:12:30,115
         MERRILL STARTS         
     SEARCHING THE OFFICES.     

234
00:12:30,183 --> 00:12:32,751
  I WANNA MAKE SURE I CAN FIND  
        AT LEAST ONE GUN.       

235
00:12:32,819 --> 00:12:35,019
      - PARKER, YOU CALLED?     
             - YEAH.            

236
00:12:35,088 --> 00:12:36,721
            STAN, YOU           
       AND THE DESK SARGE,      

237
00:12:36,790 --> 00:12:38,957
 YOU'RE THE ONLY ONE WITH ACCESS
  TO THE EVIDENCE ROOM, RIGHT?  

238
00:12:39,025 --> 00:12:40,792
            - RIGHT.            
     - BOOK THIS IN EVIDENCE    

239
00:12:40,861 --> 00:12:42,227
      AND KEEP IT THAT WAY.     

240
00:12:42,295 --> 00:12:43,928
          - YOU GOT IT.         

241
00:12:53,006 --> 00:12:55,273
         - CAN YOU TELL         
     WHAT'S HAPPENED TO HIM?    

242
00:12:55,342 --> 00:12:57,442
     - WELL, IT'S STRANGE--     

243
00:12:57,511 --> 00:13:00,812
      THIS, UM, DARK BLOOD.     

244
00:13:00,881 --> 00:13:03,948
  I KNOW WHAT YOUR CHIEF SAID,  
      BUT CHEMICAL WEAPONS,     

245
00:13:04,017 --> 00:13:05,416
    THEY DON'T ACT LIKE THIS.   

246
00:13:05,485 --> 00:13:07,819
  - DO YOU THINK IT'S A VIRUS?  
              - NO.             

247
00:13:07,888 --> 00:13:10,388
     NO, VIRUSES DON'T MOVE     
    WITH THIS KIND OF SPEED.    

248
00:13:10,457 --> 00:13:12,891
    IT'S NOT LIKE ANY POISON    
         I'VE EVER SEEN.        

249
00:13:12,959 --> 00:13:15,293
        IT'S LIKE NOTHING       
  IN THE KNOWN MEDICAL RECORD.  

250
00:13:15,362 --> 00:13:17,395
     - ALL RIGHT. THANK YOU,    
         DR. UNDERWOOD.         

251
00:13:17,464 --> 00:13:19,964
      - HEY, CALL ME HUGH.      

252
00:13:22,569 --> 00:13:25,470
     - I DON'T THINK HAVEN'S    
  IN THE KNOWN MEDICAL RECORD.  

253
00:13:25,539 --> 00:13:26,938
         - IT'S GOTTA BE        
          THE TROUBLES.         

254
00:13:27,007 --> 00:13:30,141
      - SO WHOSE AFFLICTION     
   IS SPREADING THIS DISEASE?   

255
00:13:31,678 --> 00:13:34,579
    - THE PERSON IS PROBABLY    
      STILL IN THE STATION.     

256
00:13:34,648 --> 00:13:37,949
 THEY COULD BE INFECTING WHOEVER
 THEY'RE COMING IN CONTACT WITH.

257
00:13:38,018 --> 00:13:40,451
    - OKAY, SO THIS HAPPENED,   
   WHAT, ABOUT 45 MINUTES AGO,  

258
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:42,120
      AND WE'VE ALREADY GOT     
           A NEW CASE?          

259
00:13:42,189 --> 00:13:43,421
    THAT MEANS THAT ALL OF US   
          COULD BE SICK         

260
00:13:43,490 --> 00:13:45,590
    WITHIN A MATTER OF HOURS.   

261
00:13:45,659 --> 00:13:47,592
       I'M GONNA GO AHEAD       
        AND CHECK ON EVI.       

262
00:13:47,661 --> 00:13:49,260
     - DWIGHT, IT'S NATHAN.     
          DO YOU READ?          

263
00:13:49,329 --> 00:13:52,163
             - WOW.             
        OUTSIDE CONTACT.        

264
00:13:52,232 --> 00:13:54,999
         I'M GONNA TELL         
      THE NEW CHIEF ON YOU.     

265
00:14:00,006 --> 00:14:01,272
            - DWIGHT.           

266
00:14:01,341 --> 00:14:02,640
       - IT'S ABOUT TIME.       

267
00:14:02,709 --> 00:14:03,942
         WHAT THE HELL'S        
       GOING ON UP THERE?       

268
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:05,610
       - WE GOT SOME KIND       
        OF OUTBREAK HERE.       

269
00:14:05,679 --> 00:14:07,078
         - MY BUDDY FROM        
    THE STATE POLICE CALLED.    

270
00:14:07,147 --> 00:14:08,413
     SAID THEY GOT A TIPOFF.    

271
00:14:08,481 --> 00:14:10,048
       ANY CALL FROM HAVEN      
           IS A PRANK.          

272
00:14:10,116 --> 00:14:11,883
           C.D.C. GOT           
        THE SAME WARNING.       

273
00:14:11,952 --> 00:14:14,052
 I FIGURED THERE WERE SOMETHING 
 YOU WERE TRYING TO KEEP QUIET. 

274
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:17,188
   - NO, I GUESS SOMEBODY IS.   

275
00:14:17,257 --> 00:14:19,023
    WE'RE CUT OFF COMPLETELY.   

276
00:14:19,092 --> 00:14:20,491
         - THINK SOMEONE        
          PLANNED THIS?         

277
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:22,493
    - I DON'T KNOW. JUST STAY   
     BY THE RADIO RIGHT NOW.    

278
00:14:22,562 --> 00:14:25,263
     YOU'RE MY ONLY BACKUP.     
          - ROGER THAT.         

279
00:14:32,505 --> 00:14:34,439
    - HEY. I CHECKED ON EVI.    
      SHE'S GETTING WORSE.      

280
00:14:34,507 --> 00:14:36,474
   AND NOW THIS OTHER WOMAN'S   
           GOT IT TOO.          

281
00:14:36,543 --> 00:14:39,611
      - SOMEBODY CALLED OFF     
 THE STATE POLICE AND THE C.D.C.

282
00:14:39,679 --> 00:14:41,212
          - WHAT? WHY?          

283
00:14:41,281 --> 00:14:45,383
      - I'M MORE INTERESTED     
    IN WHO WANTS US CUT OFF.    

284
00:14:45,452 --> 00:14:47,886
         - DO YOU THINK         
    THAT MERRILL'S TROUBLED?    

285
00:14:47,954 --> 00:14:50,989
 - YOU DON'T THINK THE REV WOULD
   VET HIS NEW PICK FOR CHIEF?  

286
00:14:51,057 --> 00:14:52,991
   - OKAY, LOOK, IT'S NOT LIKE  
   THERE'S A TEST, ALL RIGHT?   

287
00:14:53,059 --> 00:14:55,727
     MAYBE HE'S ISOLATING US    
      TO COVER HIS TRACKS.      

288
00:14:55,795 --> 00:14:58,730
      - WE GOTTA BE SMART,      
 TRY AND REASON WITH HIM FIRST. 

289
00:15:01,201 --> 00:15:02,600
          - ANY PERSON          
      LEAVING THIS BUILDING     

290
00:15:02,669 --> 00:15:03,935
     WILL BE SHOT ON SIGHT.     

291
00:15:04,004 --> 00:15:06,204
         - SHOT? BY WHO?        

292
00:15:06,273 --> 00:15:07,906
     - THIS IS AN OUTBREAK.     

293
00:15:07,974 --> 00:15:10,642
    IT NEEDS TO BE CONTAINED.   

294
00:15:10,710 --> 00:15:12,343
       THERE ARE ARMED MEN      
      OUTSIDE THIS BUILDING     

295
00:15:12,412 --> 00:15:14,178
      WHO WILL SHOOT ANYONE     
          SEEN LEAVING,         

296
00:15:14,247 --> 00:15:16,848
  AND THEY WILL ONLY STAND DOWN 
          ON MY ORDER.          

297
00:15:16,917 --> 00:15:18,349
     - WHO THE HELL ARE YOU?    

298
00:15:18,418 --> 00:15:21,052
     - I'M THE GUY BRINGING     
    THIS PLACE UNDER CONTROL.   

299
00:15:22,389 --> 00:15:24,022
          - OKAY, SIR,          

300
00:15:24,090 --> 00:15:26,124
    HAVE YOU EVER CONSIDERED    
         THE POSSIBILITY        

301
00:15:26,192 --> 00:15:28,359
        THAT MAYBE YOU'RE       
      THE ONE CAUSING THIS?     

302
00:15:28,428 --> 00:15:30,862
           - YOU THINK          
          I'M TROUBLED?         

303
00:15:30,931 --> 00:15:34,532
          THE TROUBLED          
        ARE WHY I'M HERE.       

304
00:15:34,601 --> 00:15:36,401
  PEOPLE ARE SICK AND TIRED OF  
 A TOWN THAT LOOKS THE OTHER WAY

305
00:15:36,469 --> 00:15:38,403
       WHILE THE TROUBLED       
         BREAK THE LAW.         

306
00:15:38,471 --> 00:15:40,538
   - THE REV BROUGHT YOU HERE,  
           DIDN'T HE?           

307
00:15:40,607 --> 00:15:42,540
           - I'M HERE           
      TO ENFORCE THE LAW...     

308
00:15:42,609 --> 00:15:44,042
          - OH, MY GOD.         
             CHIEF.             

309
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:45,777
     - TO TREAT THE TROUBLED    
       FOR WHAT THEY ARE--      

310
00:15:45,845 --> 00:15:47,245
           CRIMINALS!           

311
00:15:47,314 --> 00:15:49,247
             WE HAVE            
       TO MAINTAIN ORDER.       

312
00:15:49,316 --> 00:15:51,416
             WE HAVE            
        TO CONTAIN THIS.        

313
00:15:51,484 --> 00:15:54,485
            NO ONE IS           
      LEAVING HERE UNTIL...     

314
00:16:01,227 --> 00:16:02,593
            [coughs]            

315
00:16:04,664 --> 00:16:06,864
          OH, DAMN IT.          

316
00:16:07,867 --> 00:16:10,234
      YOUR KIND WON'T WIN.      

317
00:16:11,871 --> 00:16:13,371
             [thud]             

318
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,720
     - FOR NOW JUST GO AHEAD    
   AND PUT HIM IN THE BATHROOM  

319
00:16:28,788 --> 00:16:30,321
           WITH PAUL.           

320
00:16:30,390 --> 00:16:31,723
     - MERRILL'S CELL PHONE.    

321
00:16:31,791 --> 00:16:33,858
    IT'S PASSWORD-PROTECTED,    
           OF COURSE.           

322
00:16:33,927 --> 00:16:36,060
      BUT HE MUST'VE KNOWN      
HE WAS INFECTED THIS WHOLE TIME.

323
00:16:36,129 --> 00:16:37,996
       MAYBE HE REALLY DID      
   WANNA CONTAIN THE OUTBREAK.  

324
00:16:38,064 --> 00:16:41,666
    - OR HE WAS TERRIFIED BY    
 WHOEVER WAS GIVING HIM ORDERS. 

325
00:16:41,735 --> 00:16:44,002
      - DWIGHT, DO YOU SEE      
       ANYBODY OUT THERE?       

326
00:16:44,070 --> 00:16:45,403
         - AFFIRMATIVE.         

327
00:16:45,472 --> 00:16:47,005
      I'M NOT THE ONLY ONE      
      WATCHING THE STATION.     

328
00:16:47,073 --> 00:16:49,440
 YOU GOT TWO ARMED WITH HANDGUNS
        ON THE PERIMETER,       

329
00:16:49,509 --> 00:16:51,509
 AT LEAST ONE ON THE ROOFTOP    
     OF THE POST OFFICE         

330
00:16:51,578 --> 00:16:53,277
       ACROSS THE STREET,       
     PACKING A SNIPER RIFLE.    

331
00:16:53,346 --> 00:16:55,113
         - HEAD OVER TO         
    THE SHERIFF'S DEPARTMENT    

332
00:16:55,181 --> 00:16:56,447
         AND SEE IF YOU         
     CAN GET US SOME BACKUP.    

333
00:16:56,516 --> 00:16:57,815
           - WILL DO.           

334
00:17:04,457 --> 00:17:05,957
         - GOT MERRILL'S        
          ACCESS CARD.          

335
00:17:06,026 --> 00:17:07,792
         WE CAN OVERRIDE        
      THE ELECTRONIC LOCKS.     

336
00:17:07,861 --> 00:17:09,093
         WE CAN GET OUT         
            OF HERE.            

337
00:17:09,162 --> 00:17:11,029
           - OF COURSE          
     WE CAN'T REALLY USE IT.    

338
00:17:11,097 --> 00:17:13,698
   I MEAN, EVEN IF THESE GUYS   
   OUTSIDE ARE JUST FOR SHOW,   

339
00:17:13,767 --> 00:17:14,932
          WE CAN'T LET          
         THIS THING OUT.        

340
00:17:15,001 --> 00:17:16,467
        IT COULD WIPE OUT       
          ALL OF HAVEN.         

341
00:17:16,536 --> 00:17:17,802
      - OKAY, IT LOOKS LIKE     
  THAT THIS THING KILLS PEOPLE  

342
00:17:17,871 --> 00:17:19,137
         IN A FEW HOURS,        

343
00:17:19,205 --> 00:17:20,772
     SO WE REALLY DON'T HAVE    
         THAT MUCH TIME.        

344
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:22,306
      I'M PROBABLY IMMUNE.      

345
00:17:22,375 --> 00:17:25,309
      I'M JUST GONNA START      
 INTERVIEWING PEOPLE ONE BY ONE.

346
00:17:25,378 --> 00:17:27,912
          - EXCEPT EVI.         
           SHE'S MINE.          

347
00:17:30,350 --> 00:17:32,583
         - I NEED TO GET        
         TO A HOSPITAL.         

348
00:17:32,652 --> 00:17:34,986
         - WE CAN'T RISK        
     LETTING YOU OUT THERE.     

349
00:17:35,055 --> 00:17:37,755
          WE DON'T KNOW         
      IF YOU'RE CONTAGIOUS.     

350
00:17:39,192 --> 00:17:41,092
           WHOA, WHOA.          

351
00:17:49,736 --> 00:17:52,003
              EVI.              

352
00:17:52,072 --> 00:17:55,373
   THAT'S NOT THE ONLY REASON   
          WHY I'M HERE.         

353
00:17:57,143 --> 00:17:59,077
         I NEED TO KNOW         
       WHY YOU SOLD ME OUT      

354
00:17:59,145 --> 00:18:00,578
        TO THE SELECTMEN,       

355
00:18:00,647 --> 00:18:02,613
     GOT ME FIRED AS CHIEF.     

356
00:18:02,682 --> 00:18:04,782
       WHY ARE YOU WORKING      
          WITH THE REV?         

357
00:18:04,851 --> 00:18:06,317
      - HOW'D YOU FIND OUT?     

358
00:18:06,386 --> 00:18:08,686
             - DUKE.            

359
00:18:08,755 --> 00:18:10,922
    HE SAW YOUR TEXT MESSAGE.   

360
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:16,761
     - THAT'S WHY HE'S BEEN     
       ACTING SO STRANGE.       

361
00:18:16,830 --> 00:18:18,863
              LOOK,             
      THIS WASN'T PERSONAL.     

362
00:18:18,932 --> 00:18:21,032
      I--I GOT IN TOO DEEP.     

363
00:18:21,101 --> 00:18:22,834
  AND THAT'S WHEN THEY ASKED ME 
        TO DO THAT THING        

364
00:18:22,902 --> 00:18:24,135
        WITH YOUR FILES.        

365
00:18:24,204 --> 00:18:25,803
         - WHO'S "THEY"?        
            THE REV?            

366
00:18:25,872 --> 00:18:27,271
       - HE'S ONE OF THEM.      

367
00:18:27,340 --> 00:18:30,708
    - WHY IS IT SO IMPORTANT    
   TO HAVE ME OUT OF THE WAY?   

368
00:18:30,777 --> 00:18:33,111
     - BECAUSE THEY SAID IT     
     WOULD BE HELPING DUKE.     

369
00:18:33,179 --> 00:18:34,879
       - EXPLAIN IT TO ME.      
           - I CAN'T.           

370
00:18:34,948 --> 00:18:37,381
        - THEN EXPLAIN IT       
             TO ME.             

371
00:18:52,198 --> 00:18:53,631
          - I'M SORRY.          
           THESE MEN,           

372
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:55,533
         THEY SAID THAT         
       I'D BE HELPING YOU.      

373
00:18:55,602 --> 00:18:58,069
 - HOW DOES GETTING NATHAN FIRED
        POSSIBLY HELP ME?       

374
00:18:58,138 --> 00:18:59,370
       - I--I DON'T KNOW,       
              OKAY?             

375
00:18:59,439 --> 00:19:02,140
       THEY SAID THAT YOU       
         WERE IMPORTANT,        

376
00:19:02,208 --> 00:19:03,975
       AND THAT YOU NEEDED      
    TO LEARN CERTAIN THINGS,    

377
00:19:04,043 --> 00:19:06,444
     AND NATHAN NEEDED TO BE    
         OUT OF THE WAY         

378
00:19:06,513 --> 00:19:07,879
         BECAUSE IT'D BE        
       A PROBLEM FOR YOU.       

379
00:19:07,947 --> 00:19:09,881
            - [sighs]           

380
00:19:18,091 --> 00:19:21,726
       HOW NAIVE ARE YOU?       

381
00:19:23,596 --> 00:19:25,363
    OR DID THEY JUST PAY YOU    
         A LOT OF MONEY?        

382
00:19:25,431 --> 00:19:27,198
          - OH, MY GOD.         
    IT'S NOT ABOUT THE MONEY.   

383
00:19:27,267 --> 00:19:28,699
     I BELIEVED THEM, OKAY?     

384
00:19:28,768 --> 00:19:31,235
     I BELIEVED THEM BECAUSE    
     THEY TOLD ME SOMETHING     

385
00:19:31,304 --> 00:19:33,271
       THAT I ALWAYS KNEW.      

386
00:19:33,339 --> 00:19:34,605
         YOU'RE SPECIAL.        

387
00:19:34,674 --> 00:19:36,440
            - MM-HMM.           

388
00:19:36,509 --> 00:19:39,177
        AND WHAT MAKES ME       
           SO SPECIAL?          

389
00:19:39,245 --> 00:19:40,545
          - ALL I KNOW          

390
00:19:40,613 --> 00:19:42,914
   IS THAT WHATEVER'S GOING ON  
          IN THIS TOWN,         

391
00:19:42,982 --> 00:19:44,549
     THEY THINK THAT YOU'RE     
      IN THE MIDDLE OF IT.      

392
00:19:44,617 --> 00:19:48,085
        - WHAT? TELL ME!        
            TELL ME!            

393
00:19:48,154 --> 00:19:50,721
   - I CAN'T! I'M TELLING YOU   
          WHAT I KNOW!          

394
00:19:50,790 --> 00:19:53,090
       - AFTER EVERYTHING,      
  YOU OWE ME SOME REAL ANSWERS. 

395
00:19:53,159 --> 00:19:55,226
            - [sighs]           
           - SO WHAT?           

396
00:19:55,295 --> 00:19:57,061
        EVERYTHING THAT'S       
       HAPPENED BETWEEN US      

397
00:19:57,130 --> 00:19:58,596
         WAS CONTROLLED         
            BY THEM.            

398
00:19:58,665 --> 00:20:02,567
            - NO. NO.           
        - YOU COULD DIE.        

399
00:20:02,635 --> 00:20:05,503
        WE ALL COULD DIE.       

400
00:20:05,572 --> 00:20:07,171
          THERE ARE MEN         
      OUT THERE WITH GUNS,      

401
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:09,674
           STOPPING US          
          FROM LEAVING.         

402
00:20:12,979 --> 00:20:17,381
      EVEN WITH ALL THAT...     

403
00:20:17,450 --> 00:20:20,484
         YOU STILL CAN'T        
       TELL ME THE TRUTH.       

404
00:20:29,295 --> 00:20:30,962
        [door slams shut]       

405
00:20:35,668 --> 00:20:37,702
          - [sniffles]          

406
00:20:50,683 --> 00:20:52,683
             [gasps]            

407
00:21:02,662 --> 00:21:04,295
      - UH, NIKKI COLEMAN.      

408
00:21:04,364 --> 00:21:07,598
    I CAME IN TO FILE A, UH,    
  BUILDING PERMIT FOR MY BOSS.  

409
00:21:07,667 --> 00:21:09,333
         - OKAY, GREAT.         
    AND DID YOU TALK TO, UH,    

410
00:21:09,402 --> 00:21:11,469
          CHIEF MERRILL         
        OR OFFICER STARK?       

411
00:21:11,537 --> 00:21:12,937
    - I TALKED WITH EVERYONE.   

412
00:21:13,006 --> 00:21:15,039
      THEY KEPT TELLING ME      
     TO FILL OUT MORE FORMS.    

413
00:21:15,108 --> 00:21:16,741
         DOES THIS MEAN         
         WE CAN GO NOW?         

414
00:21:16,809 --> 00:21:18,276
          - YEAH, SOON.         

415
00:21:18,344 --> 00:21:20,344
    UM, CAN YOU JUST GO AHEAD   
  AND SEND IN THE NEXT PERSON?  

416
00:21:20,413 --> 00:21:22,813
             - YEAH.            

417
00:21:25,385 --> 00:21:27,351
            - [sighs]           

418
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:29,186
       THIS IS RIDICULOUS.      

419
00:21:29,255 --> 00:21:30,955
          DO WE REALLY          
        HAVE TO DO THIS?        

420
00:21:31,024 --> 00:21:32,623
        - WELL, YOU KNOW        
    I CAN'T MAKE IT LOOK LIKE   

421
00:21:32,692 --> 00:21:34,492
         YOU'RE GETTING         
       SPECIAL TREATMENT.       

422
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:37,028
      - FINE. I'LL MAKE IT      
          EASY FOR YA.          

423
00:21:37,096 --> 00:21:39,096
          IT'S NOT ME.          
          NOW CAN I GO?         

424
00:21:39,165 --> 00:21:40,765
     I'VE GOT A KILLER GAME     
       OF SOLITAIRE GOING.      

425
00:21:40,833 --> 00:21:42,600
     IT'S THE ONLY CARD GAME    
    WHERE NOBODY LETS ME WIN.   

426
00:21:42,669 --> 00:21:45,403
      - HAVE YOU SEEN EVI?      
 SHE'S MISSING. DUKE'S WORRIED. 

427
00:21:45,471 --> 00:21:48,306
        - WELL, SHE CAN'T       
          BE THAT FAR.          

428
00:21:48,374 --> 00:21:51,242
      - THE KEYCARD'S GONE.     
        EVI MUST HAVE IT.       

429
00:21:54,747 --> 00:21:56,847
         [scanner beeps]        

430
00:22:00,653 --> 00:22:03,020
        - WHERE ARE YOU?        

431
00:22:03,089 --> 00:22:04,689
             - EVI.             
    - I KNOW YOU'RE OUT HERE!   

432
00:22:04,757 --> 00:22:06,257
            COME ON!            
          - EVI, STOP!          

433
00:22:06,326 --> 00:22:08,559
        PLEASE, JUST COME       
          BACK INSIDE.          

434
00:22:08,628 --> 00:22:11,028
         - NO. I GOT OUT        
            FOR YOU.            

435
00:22:11,097 --> 00:22:14,365
      I COULD RUN, BUT I'M      
     NOT GONNA RUN ANYMORE.     

436
00:22:14,434 --> 00:22:17,101
      IF YOU WANT ANSWERS,      
   I'LL GET YOU YOUR ANSWERS.   

437
00:22:19,305 --> 00:22:20,304
             - EVI!             

438
00:22:20,373 --> 00:22:21,539
         [scanner beeps]        

439
00:22:21,607 --> 00:22:23,407
   - GO BACK TO THE BUILDING.   
              - NO!             

440
00:22:23,476 --> 00:22:25,543
      YOU'RE GONNA TELL HIM     
     WHAT HE WANTS TO KNOW--    

441
00:22:25,611 --> 00:22:28,379
            [gunshot]           
             - EVI!             

442
00:22:28,448 --> 00:22:29,680
          [rifle cocks]         

443
00:22:29,749 --> 00:22:31,282
        - HOLD YOUR FIRE!       
            NOT HIM!            

444
00:22:38,825 --> 00:22:41,659
        - YOU'RE GONNA BE       
           ALL RIGHT.           

445
00:22:48,234 --> 00:22:50,534
           - OH, GOD.           

446
00:22:50,603 --> 00:22:53,404
          I'M GONNA GO          
         GET SOME HELP.         

447
00:22:53,473 --> 00:22:54,739
      - [breathes heavily]      

448
00:22:54,807 --> 00:22:56,674
      WHY DID YOU DO THAT?      

449
00:22:58,177 --> 00:23:00,277
         - I'M SO SORRY.        

450
00:23:00,346 --> 00:23:04,882
           - HANG ON.           
       HELP'S ON THE WAY.       

451
00:23:45,691 --> 00:23:48,592
      - [breathing heavily]     
       - NO, NO. NO, DUKE.      

452
00:23:48,661 --> 00:23:50,327
         NOT LIKE THIS.         

453
00:23:51,364 --> 00:23:53,164
       - IF YOU WERE EVER       
           MY FRIEND--          

454
00:23:53,232 --> 00:23:55,833
 - YOU CAN'T JUST RUN OUT THERE!
      BE SMARTER THAN THAT.     

455
00:23:55,902 --> 00:23:57,835
     - NATHAN, GET THE HELL     
         OUT OF MY WAY!         

456
00:23:57,904 --> 00:24:01,572
             - DUKE!            
         - AUDREY, YOU--        

457
00:24:03,209 --> 00:24:04,542
            - NATHAN!           

458
00:24:05,912 --> 00:24:08,679
    - I JUST SAVED HIS LIFE.    

459
00:24:08,748 --> 00:24:10,848
       - ALL RIGHT, WELL,       
     I'M GONNA GO FIGURE OUT    

460
00:24:10,917 --> 00:24:12,917
        HOW TO STOP THIS.       

461
00:24:22,662 --> 00:24:24,295
       [drawer bangs shut]      

462
00:24:41,247 --> 00:24:43,614
         NIKKI COLEMAN.         

463
00:24:44,917 --> 00:24:46,851
     YOU DIDN'T MENTION THAT    
    OFFICER STARK MADE A CALL   

464
00:24:46,919 --> 00:24:48,652
        TO YOUR RESIDENCE       
         EARLIER TODAY,         

465
00:24:48,721 --> 00:24:51,088
       THAT YOU WERE ALSO       
   IN CHIEF MERRILL'S OFFICE.   

466
00:24:51,157 --> 00:24:52,756
    AND NOW THEY'RE BOTH DEAD   

467
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:54,692
        THREE HOURS AFTER       
       THEY TALKED TO YOU.      

468
00:24:54,760 --> 00:24:56,026
     - I--I WANNA HELP YOU,     

469
00:24:56,095 --> 00:24:58,996
       BUT I CAN'T BE SEEN      
         TALKING TO YOU.        

470
00:24:59,065 --> 00:25:00,064
        [knocks on door]        
            - AUDREY.           

471
00:25:00,132 --> 00:25:01,465
        - CHRIS, NOT NOW.       

472
00:25:01,534 --> 00:25:03,100
     - THEN I GUESS I WON'T     
      BOTHER YOU WITH THIS.     

473
00:25:03,169 --> 00:25:05,903
         - HELLO AGAIN.         
              - HI.             

474
00:25:05,972 --> 00:25:08,672
   - YOU TALKED TO NIKKI TOO?   
    - YEAH, SHE TALKED TO ME.   

475
00:25:08,741 --> 00:25:11,141
              WHY?              

476
00:25:11,210 --> 00:25:12,376
         SHE'S THE ONE?         

477
00:25:12,445 --> 00:25:14,845
  BE A DOLL AND CLEAR THIS UP,  
            WILL YA?            

478
00:25:14,914 --> 00:25:16,547
         DO THAT VOODOO         
          THAT YOU DO.          

479
00:25:16,616 --> 00:25:18,349
      - I DON'T UNDERSTAND.     

480
00:25:18,417 --> 00:25:20,684
        - YOU'RE THE ONE        
  THAT'S CAUSING THIS DISEASE,  

481
00:25:20,753 --> 00:25:21,986
         SO JUST FIX IT,        
            WILL YOU?           

482
00:25:22,054 --> 00:25:23,153
             - OKAY.            

483
00:25:23,222 --> 00:25:25,055
         I HAVEN'T EVEN         
          TOLD HER YET.         

484
00:25:25,124 --> 00:25:26,423
          - I'M DYING.          

485
00:25:26,492 --> 00:25:27,691
      GIVE ME FIVE MINUTES      
       WITH PATIENT ZERO.       

486
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:29,460
  I'LL HAVE HER HEALING LEPERS. 
          LOOK AT HER.          

487
00:25:29,529 --> 00:25:31,328
        SHE'S PRACTICALLY       
        IN LOVE WITH ME.        

488
00:25:31,397 --> 00:25:33,197
   - WHAT HAS HAPPENED TO YOU?  
   YOU'VE COMPLETELY CHANGED.   

489
00:25:33,266 --> 00:25:34,865
        - YEAH, WHATEVER.       
   I'M GOING TO THE HOSPITAL.   

490
00:25:34,934 --> 00:25:37,301
  - NO, YOU CAN'T LEAVE, OKAY?  
PEOPLE OUT THERE WILL SHOOT YOU.

491
00:25:37,370 --> 00:25:39,136
   - NOBODY WANTS TO SHOOT ME.  
            - REALLY?           

492
00:25:39,205 --> 00:25:41,438
       YOU'RE A SCIENTIST.      
  TELL ME, WHAT WORKS FASTER--  

493
00:25:41,507 --> 00:25:42,806
    YOUR TROUBLE OR A BULLET?   

494
00:25:42,875 --> 00:25:44,975
     LISTEN, I CAN SAVE YOU     

495
00:25:45,044 --> 00:25:46,610
 IF YOU JUST LET ME GET THROUGH 
      TO THIS VERY SCARED,      

496
00:25:46,679 --> 00:25:48,779
     AND NOW, THANKS TO YOU,    
      VERY CONFUSED WOMAN.      

497
00:25:48,848 --> 00:25:50,781
           ALL RIGHT?           
     JUST LET ME DO MY JOB.     

498
00:25:50,850 --> 00:25:53,484
   - MAN, I WISH MY AFFLICTION  
         WORKED ON YOU.         

499
00:25:55,688 --> 00:25:57,288
       - USUALLY A TROUBLE      
           LIKE YOURS           

500
00:25:57,356 --> 00:25:59,290
          IS TRIGGERED          
      BY A TRAUMATIC EVENT.     

501
00:25:59,358 --> 00:26:02,126
     DID SOMETHING LIKE THAT    
        HAPPEN RECENTLY?        

502
00:26:05,598 --> 00:26:07,965
             PLEASE.            
        YOU CAN TELL ME.        

503
00:26:08,034 --> 00:26:09,967
         - NO, LIKE, I--        

504
00:26:10,036 --> 00:26:13,704
         YOU DON'T SEE--        
    I--I CAN'T SAY ANYTHING.    

505
00:26:14,941 --> 00:26:16,373
           HE'S BACK.           

506
00:26:16,442 --> 00:26:20,177
    AND HE'LL HURT ME AGAIN,    
          KILL ME EVEN.         

507
00:26:20,246 --> 00:26:23,280
        - IS THAT WHY YOU       
      CALLED OFFICER STARK?     

508
00:26:23,349 --> 00:26:25,983
    IS THAT WHY YOU CAME DOWN   
         TO THE STATION?        

509
00:26:26,052 --> 00:26:28,953
         BECAUSE YOU'RE         
          BEING ABUSED?         

510
00:26:35,194 --> 00:26:37,294
     OKAY, LISTEN, THAT MAN     
     THAT YOU'RE AFRAID OF,     

511
00:26:37,363 --> 00:26:39,263
     HE CAN'T HURT YOU HERE,    
           ALL RIGHT?           

512
00:26:39,332 --> 00:26:40,631
          YOU'RE SAFE.          

513
00:26:40,700 --> 00:26:42,967
      - NO, I'M NEVER SAFE.     

514
00:26:43,035 --> 00:26:45,135
    YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND. I--   

515
00:26:45,204 --> 00:26:47,705
        IT TOOK ME YEARS.       

516
00:26:47,773 --> 00:26:51,208
           I RAN AWAY.          
       I CHANGED MY NAME.       

517
00:26:52,511 --> 00:26:54,311
       TODAY HE FOUND ME.       

518
00:26:55,715 --> 00:26:57,314
       HE SAID IF I TALKED      
          TO THE POLICE         

519
00:26:57,383 --> 00:26:59,750
         HE'LL KILL ME.         

520
00:27:00,786 --> 00:27:03,053
            - [sighs]           

521
00:27:03,122 --> 00:27:04,788
         UH, EXCUSE ME.         

522
00:27:04,857 --> 00:27:07,992
             UM, HI.            
       I'M HUGH UNDERWOOD.      

523
00:27:08,060 --> 00:27:09,994
          I'M A DOCTOR.         
      - YEAH, CHRIS BRODY.      

524
00:27:10,062 --> 00:27:12,830
      I'D SHAKE YOUR HAND,      
   BUT I'M PRETTY MUCH DYING.   

525
00:27:12,898 --> 00:27:14,298
        - AH, I'M SORRY,        
             CHRIS.             

526
00:27:14,367 --> 00:27:16,834
   UM, I JUST SAW YOU IN THERE  
       WITH THE DETECTIVE       

527
00:27:16,902 --> 00:27:18,535
            AND THAT,           
        UM, NIKKI WOMAN.        

528
00:27:18,604 --> 00:27:19,803
        WHAT'S GOING ON?        

529
00:27:19,872 --> 00:27:21,271
        - MY GIRLFRIEND,        
       OR WHATEVER SHE IS,      

530
00:27:21,340 --> 00:27:22,506
         DOESN'T WANT ME        
            TO LEAVE.           

531
00:27:22,575 --> 00:27:23,741
      SHE'S THE DETECTIVE.      

532
00:27:23,809 --> 00:27:25,376
         SHE'S IN THERE         
       CHATTING UP A STORM      

533
00:27:25,444 --> 00:27:27,011
       WHILE I'M OUT HERE       
             DYING.             

534
00:27:27,079 --> 00:27:29,046
        - I MIGHT BE ABLE       
          TO HELP YOU.          

535
00:27:29,115 --> 00:27:30,814
        IF I CAN GET YOU        
    TO THE HOSPITAL IN TIME,    

536
00:27:30,883 --> 00:27:33,517
         I MIGHT BE ABLE        
       TO SAVE YOUR LIFE.       

537
00:27:33,586 --> 00:27:35,185
       THE ONLY THING IS,       
         THERE'S NO WAY         

538
00:27:35,254 --> 00:27:37,187
      THEY'RE GONNA LET US      
     OUT OF HERE OTHERWISE.     

539
00:27:37,256 --> 00:27:39,189
     WE'RE GONNA NEED A GUN     
          OR SOMETHING.         

540
00:27:43,863 --> 00:27:46,230
       - IT'S STAN, RIGHT?      

541
00:27:46,298 --> 00:27:48,432
         - YEAH. THANKS         
        FOR REMEMBERING.        

542
00:27:48,501 --> 00:27:49,933
             - YEAH.            

543
00:27:50,002 --> 00:27:53,170
   UM, STAN, PARKER WANTED ME   
      TO GET THAT ENVELOPE      

544
00:27:53,239 --> 00:27:54,471
          THAT YOU PUT          
         INTO EVIDENCE.         

545
00:27:54,540 --> 00:27:55,706
             - SURE.            

546
00:28:00,913 --> 00:28:02,212
         - I THINK THAT         
       ALL OF THOSE YEARS       

547
00:28:02,281 --> 00:28:04,481
         THAT YOU SPENT         
      ABSORBING THAT ABUSE,     

548
00:28:04,550 --> 00:28:06,517
     SWALLOWING THAT POISON,    

549
00:28:06,585 --> 00:28:08,385
          I THINK TODAY         
        WHEN HE SHOWED UP       

550
00:28:08,454 --> 00:28:10,788
     IT FINALLY LEAKED OUT.     

551
00:28:10,856 --> 00:28:13,490
       IT'S BEEN INFECTING      
        ALL THESE PEOPLE.       

552
00:28:14,460 --> 00:28:16,126
         LISTEN, IF YOU         
       TELL ME WHO HE IS,       

553
00:28:16,195 --> 00:28:18,462
      WE CAN CONFRONT HIM,      

554
00:28:18,531 --> 00:28:20,064
          AND MAYBE WE          
       CAN END THIS THING.      

555
00:28:20,132 --> 00:28:22,533
            - HE'S--            
       HE KNOWS I'M HERE.       

556
00:28:22,601 --> 00:28:24,401
            HE KNOWS            
       I'M TALKING TO YOU.      

557
00:28:24,470 --> 00:28:28,405
  - NO. HOW WOULD HE KNOW THAT  
         UNLESS HE'S...         

558
00:28:28,474 --> 00:28:30,074
              HERE.             

559
00:28:30,142 --> 00:28:32,376
            - [gasps]           

560
00:28:32,445 --> 00:28:34,111
      - EXCUSE ME, OFFICER.     

561
00:28:34,180 --> 00:28:36,313
         MIND IF I HAVE         
      A WORD WITH MY WIFE?      

562
00:28:44,924 --> 00:28:47,357
        - GET OVER THERE.       
     - ALL RIGHT, ALL RIGHT.    

563
00:28:47,426 --> 00:28:50,027
     OKAY, YOU'RE IN CHARGE.    

564
00:28:51,897 --> 00:28:54,431
          - YES, I AM.          

565
00:29:00,773 --> 00:29:03,440
        I'VE HEARD ABOUT        
      THE FREAKS IN HAVEN.      

566
00:29:06,979 --> 00:29:10,380
   BUT CREATING A PESTILENCE?   

567
00:29:10,449 --> 00:29:11,915
       - YOU DON'T HAVE TO      
         DO THIS, HUGH.         

568
00:29:11,984 --> 00:29:14,051
        - WELL, NOW I DO,       
            DON'T I?            

569
00:29:14,120 --> 00:29:16,520
           BECAUSE SHE          
      COMPLAINED ABOUT ME.      

570
00:29:16,589 --> 00:29:18,989
         - SHE DIDN'T DO        
         ANYTHING WRONG.        

571
00:29:19,058 --> 00:29:21,191
            - [sobs]            

572
00:29:21,260 --> 00:29:23,861
          - SHE DID DO          
        ONE THING RIGHT.        

573
00:29:23,929 --> 00:29:26,463
     SHE GAVE EVERYONE ELSE     
     THE DISEASE EXCEPT ME,     

574
00:29:26,532 --> 00:29:28,665
             AND NOW            
       THEY'RE ALL DYING.       

575
00:29:28,734 --> 00:29:30,200
            MAYBE...            

576
00:29:30,269 --> 00:29:32,736
        THAT'S BECAUSE...       

577
00:29:32,805 --> 00:29:34,605
           YOU KNOW...          

578
00:29:34,673 --> 00:29:38,509
      I'M THE ONLY ONE WHO      
   TRULY UNDERSTANDS YOU, HUH?  

579
00:29:40,713 --> 00:29:43,313
             - HEY.             

580
00:29:43,382 --> 00:29:44,915
              HUGH.             

581
00:29:44,984 --> 00:29:46,583
             BUDDY.             

582
00:29:46,652 --> 00:29:48,552
     LET'S TALK ABOUT THIS.     

583
00:29:48,621 --> 00:29:50,087
           - SIT DOWN.          
   YOU'VE ALREADY DONE ENOUGH.  

584
00:29:50,156 --> 00:29:52,623
  YOU ALREADY GAVE HIM MY GUN.  
             - HEY!             

585
00:29:52,691 --> 00:29:54,925
      DON'T YOU TALK TO HIM     
           LIKE THAT.           

586
00:29:58,564 --> 00:30:01,031
      MAYBE YOU NEED TO BE      
    TAUGHT A LITTLE RESPECT.    

587
00:30:01,100 --> 00:30:02,566
       WHAT DO YOU THINK?       

588
00:30:05,738 --> 00:30:07,571
         WAIT A SECOND.         

589
00:30:10,042 --> 00:30:12,943
    HOW COME YOU'RE NOT SICK    
        LIKE THE OTHERS?        

590
00:30:19,385 --> 00:30:22,486
       - NATHAN, COME ON.       

591
00:30:22,555 --> 00:30:24,454
         YOU CAN'T JUST         
        LOCK ME IN HERE.        

592
00:30:24,523 --> 00:30:26,723
        I'M NOT--I'M NOT        
       GONNA DO ANYTHING.       

593
00:30:26,792 --> 00:30:28,458
  - YOU'RE NOT THINKING RIGHT.  

594
00:30:28,527 --> 00:30:31,328
     - NATHAN, I GOT BACKUP.    
 THE SHERIFF'S TEN MINUTES OUT. 

595
00:30:31,397 --> 00:30:32,696
            - GREAT.            
          - NOT GREAT.          

596
00:30:32,765 --> 00:30:34,031
      OUR BUDDIES OUT HERE      
       MUST HAVE A SCANNER      

597
00:30:34,099 --> 00:30:35,532
            AND HEARD           
        THE CALL GO OUT.        

598
00:30:35,601 --> 00:30:37,234
       THEY'RE GEARING UP.      
  LOOKS LIKE THEY'RE COMING IN. 

599
00:30:37,303 --> 00:30:39,169
    - THEY WANNA WIPE US OUT    
     BEFORE HELP GETS HERE.     

600
00:30:39,238 --> 00:30:41,371
  - THEY'RE COMING IN THE BACK. 
      I'VE GOT YOU COVERED.     

601
00:30:44,410 --> 00:30:46,677
            - NATHAN.           

602
00:30:46,745 --> 00:30:48,278
       YOU GOTTA LET ME GO      
            WITH YOU.           

603
00:30:48,347 --> 00:30:50,948
      - I'M NOT LETTING YOU     
      GET YOURSELF KILLED.      

604
00:30:51,016 --> 00:30:52,716
            - NATHAN!           

605
00:30:52,785 --> 00:30:54,718
              WAIT!             

606
00:30:54,787 --> 00:30:57,454
             NATHAN,            
      DON'T DO THIS TO ME!      

607
00:31:03,729 --> 00:31:08,031
          - I'M SORRY.          
      I CAN'T LET YOU LIVE.     

608
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:10,400
       YOU'LL KEEP ME AWAY      
         FROM MY NICOLE.        

609
00:31:10,469 --> 00:31:13,136
      - HEY, COME ON, DOC.      

610
00:31:13,205 --> 00:31:15,138
           I GET YOU.           

611
00:31:15,207 --> 00:31:18,308
        I UNDERSTAND WHY        
       YOU'RE DOING THIS.       

612
00:31:18,377 --> 00:31:19,676
        SOMETIMES IT'S...       

613
00:31:19,745 --> 00:31:21,578
      - ISOLATING YOURSELF,     

614
00:31:21,647 --> 00:31:23,380
          FEELING WEAK,         
    THAT'S WHAT CAUSED THIS.    

615
00:31:23,449 --> 00:31:24,815
          BUT WHAT YOU          
     HAVE INSIDE OF YOU NOW,    

616
00:31:24,884 --> 00:31:26,250
            YOU NEED            
       TO TURN IT AROUND.       

617
00:31:26,318 --> 00:31:29,553
       FIGHT BACK, NIKKI.       
           - I CAN'T.           

618
00:31:29,622 --> 00:31:32,456
        - YOU DON'T WANNA       
       SEE ME DIE, DO YA?       

619
00:31:34,226 --> 00:31:35,659
      - LISTEN, YOU'RE NOT      
     JUST HURTING YOURSELF.     

620
00:31:35,728 --> 00:31:37,494
     YOU'RE HURTING EVERYONE    
        ELSE HERE, OKAY?        

621
00:31:37,563 --> 00:31:38,762
            - [sighs]           

622
00:31:38,831 --> 00:31:40,864
       - FIND THE STRENGTH      
         AND FIGHT BACK.        

623
00:31:40,933 --> 00:31:43,800
          - ALL RIGHT,          
    THAT'S ENOUGH OUT OF YOU!   

624
00:31:45,738 --> 00:31:49,373
        - STOP IT, HUGH!        

625
00:31:49,441 --> 00:31:51,775
            NO MORE.            

626
00:31:55,981 --> 00:31:59,716
       - WHAT DID YOU SAY?      
         - YOU HEARD ME.        

627
00:31:59,785 --> 00:32:01,785
         [sighs deeply]         

628
00:32:01,854 --> 00:32:03,854
        - NOW, I'M GONNA        
         COUNT TO THREE,        

629
00:32:03,923 --> 00:32:06,390
        AND YOU ARE GONNA       
        GET ON YOUR KNEES       

630
00:32:06,458 --> 00:32:08,292
         AND APOLOGIZE.         

631
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:10,427
              - NO.             

632
00:32:11,497 --> 00:32:13,797
      YOU HAVE POISONED ME      
         WITH YOUR ABUSE        

633
00:32:13,866 --> 00:32:15,799
           FOR YEARS.           

634
00:32:15,868 --> 00:32:17,801
            I'M DONE.           

635
00:32:17,870 --> 00:32:20,203
           SO KILL ME           
          IF YOU WANT.          

636
00:32:20,272 --> 00:32:22,372
        BUT I DON'T THINK       
            YOU WILL,           

637
00:32:22,441 --> 00:32:24,942
     BECAUSE YOU'RE NOTHING     
          BUT A COWARD.         

638
00:32:26,845 --> 00:32:28,912
          ROT IN HELL.          

639
00:32:30,449 --> 00:32:32,616
          - [groaning]          

640
00:32:36,622 --> 00:32:40,757
            [gasping]           

641
00:32:41,961 --> 00:32:44,928
      - [breathes heavily]      

642
00:32:48,033 --> 00:32:49,433
              I...              

643
00:32:49,501 --> 00:32:52,302
          I--I DID THAT         
             TO HIM.            

644
00:32:52,371 --> 00:32:54,271
        I--I KILLED HIM.        
              - NO.             

645
00:32:54,340 --> 00:32:56,340
      LISTEN, YOU SAVED US.     

646
00:33:01,146 --> 00:33:02,980
         HEY, IT'S OVER.        

647
00:33:04,116 --> 00:33:06,249
      - NOT FOR THOSE GUYS      
            OUTSIDE.            

648
00:33:06,318 --> 00:33:07,985
       THEY'RE COMING IN.       
             - WHY?             

649
00:33:08,053 --> 00:33:10,587
      - WIPE OUT THE CURSE      
       AND EVERYONE ELSE.       

650
00:33:12,091 --> 00:33:14,424
             - OKAY.            

651
00:33:14,493 --> 00:33:17,327
       WELL, GO STOP 'EM.       
      I'LL CALL FOR BACKUP.     

652
00:33:23,902 --> 00:33:26,436
     - DWIGHT, DO YOU COPY?     

653
00:33:27,506 --> 00:33:29,272
           [gun cocks]          

654
00:33:29,341 --> 00:33:31,641
        - THEY'RE COMING.       
            GET BACK.           

655
00:33:31,710 --> 00:33:35,812
            [gunfire]           

656
00:33:36,849 --> 00:33:40,283
         [siren wailing]        

657
00:33:40,352 --> 00:33:41,818
    - LET'S GET OUT OF HERE!    

658
00:33:41,887 --> 00:33:44,788
      [car door slams shut,     
         tires screech]         

659
00:33:44,857 --> 00:33:48,158
         [siren wailing]        

660
00:33:55,934 --> 00:33:57,467
      - [breathes heavily]      

661
00:33:57,536 --> 00:34:00,771
     - DWIGHT, YOU'RE SHOT.     

662
00:34:03,575 --> 00:34:05,375
      - ONE GRAZED MY NECK.     

663
00:34:05,444 --> 00:34:06,810
         LET ME GUESS--         

664
00:34:06,879 --> 00:34:09,446
        YOU DIDN'T CATCH        
        A SINGLE BULLET.        

665
00:34:09,515 --> 00:34:11,515
    - NOTHING HIT THE WALLS.    

666
00:34:11,583 --> 00:34:13,350
          I'M NOT HIT.          
         I DON'T GET IT.        

667
00:34:17,122 --> 00:34:21,391
        - BULLETS--THEY,        
      UH, TEND TO FIND ME.      

668
00:34:23,495 --> 00:34:24,928
       IT'S A LONG STORY.       

669
00:34:24,997 --> 00:34:28,065
         - BULLETS TEND         
          TO FIND YOU?          

670
00:34:31,003 --> 00:34:34,471
      THAT'S YOUR TROUBLE?      

671
00:34:37,509 --> 00:34:39,443
      WELL, YOU WERE RIGHT.     

672
00:34:39,511 --> 00:34:40,777
    THE WAY THINGS ARE GOING,   

673
00:34:40,846 --> 00:34:43,880
     I MIGHT NEED YOU AROUND    
         MORE THAN EVER.        

674
00:35:19,685 --> 00:35:23,253
   - I'M SORRY FOR YOUR LOSS,   
          MR. CROCKER.          

675
00:35:23,322 --> 00:35:26,423
           I TRULY AM.          

676
00:35:26,492 --> 00:35:29,693
   - SHE DIDN'T KNOW ANYTHING   
        ABOUT THIS TOWN.        

677
00:35:32,698 --> 00:35:35,432
        - SHE WAS ONE OF        
    THE MANY INNOCENT VICTIMS   

678
00:35:35,501 --> 00:35:37,167
        OF THE TROUBLED.        

679
00:35:38,704 --> 00:35:41,204
         I LOST MY WIFE         
          TO THEM TOO.          

680
00:35:47,913 --> 00:35:51,348
      - I DON'T UNDERSTAND      
          ANY OF THIS.          

681
00:35:54,386 --> 00:35:57,087
        - I CAN HELP YOU,       
          MR. CROCKER.          

682
00:36:02,227 --> 00:36:03,760
      BUT YOU'RE GONNA HAVE     
         TO PROVE TO ME         

683
00:36:03,829 --> 00:36:05,095
       THAT YOU'RE WORTHY.      

684
00:36:12,971 --> 00:36:14,371
           - REVEREND.          

685
00:36:22,581 --> 00:36:24,948
           THANK YOU.           

686
00:36:27,352 --> 00:36:29,519
      - I'LL PRAY FOR HER.      

687
00:36:45,804 --> 00:36:48,872
      - DWIGHT, I NEED YOU      
     TO DO SOMETHING FOR ME.    

688
00:36:48,941 --> 00:36:51,041
        EVI RYAN--MAKE IT       
       LOOK LIKE A SUICIDE      

689
00:36:51,109 --> 00:36:52,375
         OR AN ACCIDENT,        

690
00:36:52,444 --> 00:36:54,444
         JUST AS LONG AS        
       THE CASE IS CLOSED.      

691
00:36:54,513 --> 00:36:56,379
       - WE'RE NOT TALKING      
        ABOUT COVERING UP       

692
00:36:56,448 --> 00:36:58,148
      A SUPERNATURAL EVENT.     

693
00:36:58,217 --> 00:36:59,649
        THIS IS A MURDER.       

694
00:36:59,718 --> 00:37:01,017
   - WE CAN'T INVESTIGATE THIS  
      WITH THE STATE POLICE     

695
00:37:01,086 --> 00:37:02,185
   LOOKING OVER OUR SHOULDER.   

696
00:37:02,254 --> 00:37:04,054
         - EVI WAS SHOT         
          IN THE CHEST.         

697
00:37:04,122 --> 00:37:05,855
       SHE HAS BLACK VEINS      
          IN HER ARMS.          

698
00:37:05,924 --> 00:37:08,391
 THE MEDICAL EXAMINER'S NEVER-- 
          - NO PROBLEM.         

699
00:37:09,995 --> 00:37:12,495
 WOULDN'T BE THE TOUGHEST THING 
        I EVER HAD TO DO.       

700
00:37:13,799 --> 00:37:17,834
          IF IT'S OKAY          
        WITH YOU, CHIEF.        

701
00:37:21,440 --> 00:37:23,540
            - DO IT.            

702
00:37:23,609 --> 00:37:24,808
        ONE MORE THING--        

703
00:37:24,876 --> 00:37:27,444
     WE GOT CHIEF MERRILL'S     
        CELL PHONE LOGS.        

704
00:37:27,512 --> 00:37:28,845
       GUESS WHO HE TALKED      
      TO HALF A DOZEN TIMES     

705
00:37:28,914 --> 00:37:30,213
      DURING THE LOCKDOWN?      

706
00:37:30,282 --> 00:37:31,481
           - THE REV.           

707
00:37:36,822 --> 00:37:38,822
       HE'S IN THE MIDDLE       
         OF ALL OF THIS.        

708
00:38:16,328 --> 00:38:19,262
     SORRY. I GOT CAUGHT UP     
         AT WORK, SO...         

709
00:38:19,331 --> 00:38:22,432
    - LET ME GO FIRST, OKAY?    

710
00:38:22,501 --> 00:38:23,733
             [sighs]            

711
00:38:23,802 --> 00:38:27,337
          I SCREWED UP.         
             HUGELY.            

712
00:38:28,473 --> 00:38:33,376
       AND GIVING YOUR GUN      
       TO A PSYCHOPATH...       

713
00:38:33,445 --> 00:38:36,279
       THAT MAY HAVE BEEN       
    THE LEAST OF MY MISTAKES.   

714
00:38:38,016 --> 00:38:40,183
       I LOST YOUR TRUST.       

715
00:38:43,055 --> 00:38:45,355
    I THOUGHT I COULD HANDLE    
         MY AFFLICTION.         

716
00:38:45,424 --> 00:38:47,791
         - CHRIS, YOU--         
         - LAST NIGHT...        

717
00:38:47,859 --> 00:38:50,627
        I GAVE INTO IT...       

718
00:38:50,696 --> 00:38:53,029
           AND NEARLY           
       GOT PEOPLE KILLED.       

719
00:38:54,533 --> 00:38:56,800
         AND THAT THING         
       I SAID TO YOU ABOUT      

720
00:38:56,868 --> 00:38:59,636
           WISHING YOU          
        WEREN'T IMMUNE...       

721
00:38:59,705 --> 00:39:01,171
        THAT'S NOT TRUE.        

722
00:39:02,874 --> 00:39:04,574
  I WANNA BE WITH YOU, AUDREY.  

723
00:39:04,643 --> 00:39:08,044
     I NEED TO BE WITH YOU.     

724
00:39:12,784 --> 00:39:15,185
       - YOU ONCE TOLD ME,      

725
00:39:15,253 --> 00:39:19,622
           "I WANT YOU          
      BECAUSE YOU'RE YOU."      

726
00:39:22,060 --> 00:39:25,929
   WANTING ME AND NEEDING ME,   
  THEY'RE TWO DIFFERENT THINGS. 

727
00:39:28,266 --> 00:39:31,935
      I CAN'T BE THE PERSON     
       THAT KEEPS YOU YOU.      

728
00:39:36,208 --> 00:39:39,042
        YOU GOTTA DO THAT       
          ON YOUR OWN.          

729
00:39:39,111 --> 00:39:41,044
             - YEAH.            

730
00:39:42,914 --> 00:39:44,414
       - IT'S JUST YOU'D--      

731
00:39:44,483 --> 00:39:47,450
     YOU'D EVENTUALLY START     
      RESENTING ME FOR IT.      

732
00:39:49,955 --> 00:39:51,388
    - I THINK THE BEST THING    
          FOR ME TO DO          

733
00:39:51,456 --> 00:39:54,057
         IS TO JUST...GO        

734
00:39:54,126 --> 00:39:56,559
      SOMEWHERE BY MYSELF,      
     AWAY FROM OTHER PEOPLE.    

735
00:39:56,628 --> 00:39:58,228
     - NO, CHRIS, THAT'S NOT    
        WHAT I'M SAYING.        

736
00:39:58,296 --> 00:40:00,530
       - YOU KNOW, SOMEDAY      
   THE TROUBLES ARE GONNA END,  

737
00:40:00,599 --> 00:40:02,198
      AND I'M GONNA GO BACK     
        TO BEING THE GUY        

738
00:40:02,267 --> 00:40:04,701
      THAT EVERYBODY HATES.     

739
00:40:08,373 --> 00:40:11,841
    MAYBE THEN I'LL BE A GUY    
       THAT YOU CAN LOVE.       

